  "findings": [
    "Read full explorer.py/app.js/index.html/style.css/EXPLORER.md and both new focused test modules, plus complete scoped diff and maintained replay-selection snapshot adaptation.",
    "Endpoint changes are exactly route allowlist plus lazy dispatch to unchanged explain_replay. Reversing those two additions yields complete original explorer.py; admission, body framing/cap, Host/Origin, default run/replay, CLI and response serialization remain exact.",
    "Captured selection object and parsed value are used for explicit requests only. Pending double-click guard and current-selection checks cover success/catch/finally; new/empty/rejected/pending selections synchronously retire old action/status/rows/details without changing run state.",
    "All path/kind/side values use textContent or text nodes. Complete JSON side envelopes distinguish absence from null; ordered rows, cap indication, open native details and explicit local-error retry match the public contract.",
    "Original plot/render/current/export behavior remains outside the diff. New style rules are scoped to replay details and stack sides at narrow widths; status role and native summary remain accessible.",
    "Maintained HTTP tests cover whole ordinary reply preservation, exact typed value row,32-row truncation and refusal/explicit recovery. Node tests cover captured value without reread, pending double-click, retired success/finally/error, explicit retry, full ordered side values and unrelated retained run preservation.",
    "Reversing only the explicit new-widget exclusion restores the entire original replay-selection test byte-for-byte. All original assertions are retained.",
    "Guide distinguishes parsed JSON from source bytes/numeric spelling, local field comparison from causation, selected-file lifecycle and unchanged displayed run/export."
